'' A FOR loop over a UDT counter declines instead of emitting aggregate arithmetic.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/for-udt-counter.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 1 statements not lowered

'' What must NOT come back: a CONSTANT AGGREGATE, which is what the scalar FOR emitted
'' for the implicit step and is meaningless on any input. An 'icmp.sle' is NOT an
'' assertion here -- 'operator next' compares two integers in its own body, and asserting
'' its absence would fail for the right code.
